{
 "title": "Scene lighting and cameras",
 "summary": "The four light types on a Suzanne turned 90 degrees over a plane: a point light (every direction from one spot, moved to light the face, yellow, 1000 W), a sun (only its angle matters, strength 6), a spot (a cone, 1000 W, rotated to the face, light blue) and an area light (a rectangle; bigger is softer). Cameras: a second camera made orthographic, the active camera switched with Ctrl+Numpad0, the main camera at a 35-50 mm focal length. Beyond the tutorial: light linking gives each lamp only its own stage so all four stand side by side.",
